agent: # Automated Reorder-Point Alerts
  ## Problem
  Popular items sell out before anyone notices, and orders wait for stock, breaking one-day shipping.
  ## Actors
  Warehouse lead and order fulfillment staff.
  ## Current Process
  The warehouse lead manually checks stock against reorder points in a spreadsheet every Monday.
  ## Desired Change
  Automatically identify items at or below their reorder point each week and send one alert to the warehouse lead. The automation should be scheduled, preferably using GitHub Actions, without adding paid vendors.
  ## Success Measure
  No order waits on an item that was at or below its reorder point in the previous alert.
  ## Business Constraints
  No business constraints.
  ## Solution Constraints
  - **Allowed Solution Classes:** Scheduled automation
  - **Existing Platforms Required:** None
  - **Existing Platforms Preferred:** GitHub Actions
  - **Known Systems:** Spreadsheet
  - **Hosting Restrictions:** None
  - **Vendor Restrictions:** No new paid vendors
  - **Procurement Constraints:** None
  - **Regulatory Restrictions:** None
  **What would you add, correct, or remove?**
  If this is accurate, just say so. If you don't know, say “I don't know” and we'll work through it together.
user: Looks good.
